WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.540 --> 00:00:13.701
Polonius was reading in his study when Ophelia entered.

2
00:00:13.721 --> 00:00:16.382
"Oh Father," she cried.

3
00:00:16.402 --> 00:00:18.123
"I'm worried about Hamlet!

4
00:00:19.124 --> 00:00:24.246
He came to see me just now, his clothing in disarray, with a pitiful look on his face.

5
00:00:25.267 --> 00:00:27.788
He wouldn't speak; he just stared at me.

6
00:00:28.756 --> 00:00:33.300
He kept nodding his head, and he sighed so loudly his whole body shook.

7
00:00:33.880 --> 00:00:36.643
And then, still staring at me, he left!"

8
00:00:36.663 --> 00:00:39.425
"Oh dear," said Polonius.

9
00:00:39.445 --> 00:00:41.667
"Have you spoken to him harshly of late?"

10
00:00:42.808 --> 00:00:44.529
"No, but I did as you ordered."

11
00:00:45.069 --> 00:00:46.671
Ophelia hung her head in sorrow.

12
00:00:47.792 --> 00:00:49.653
"I told him I couldn't see him anymore."

13
00:00:49.673 --> 00:00:52.796
"Your rejection has made him mad, I fear.

14
00:00:53.396 --> 00:00:58.000
I must tell the king; he too has wondered about Hamlet's odd behavior lately."

15
00:00:59.104 --> 00:01:06.027
Hamlet's mother and his uncle Claudius were in the great hall with Hamlet's childhood friends Rosencrantz and Guildenstern.

16
00:01:07.187 --> 00:01:12.490
"I summoned you two to court," said the king, "because I believe something other than his father's death

17
00:01:12.610 --> 00:01:13.570
is troubling Hamlet.

18
00:01:14.731 --> 00:01:18.392
Spend time with him and report anything you find out to me."

19
00:01:18.412 --> 00:01:22.374
"You will be rewarded generously," Gertrude added.

20
00:01:22.894 --> 00:01:24.415
She was very worried about her son.

21
00:01:24.435 --> 00:01:29.109
"We shall obey your majesties," said Rosencrantz, bowing low.

22
00:01:29.129 --> 00:01:34.772
"At your service, your majesties," said Guildenstern, bowing even lower.

23
00:01:35.813 --> 00:01:37.734
Just then Polonius entered the hall.

24
00:01:37.754 --> 00:01:39.675
"Good news, my lord!

25
00:01:40.055 --> 00:01:42.216
The ambassadors have returned from Norway.

26
00:01:43.257 --> 00:01:46.038
Fortinbras has agreed not to invade our country.

27
00:01:46.539 --> 00:01:47.499
Denmark is safe."

28
00:01:48.760 --> 00:01:50.101
"Excellent," said Claudius.

29
00:01:50.121 --> 00:01:53.322
"I have more news," Polonius continued.

30
00:01:53.923 --> 00:01:56.124
"I know what is making Hamlet crazy.

31
00:01:57.280 --> 00:02:01.943
He has been courting my daughter, Ophelia, and I told her she should discourage him.

32
00:02:03.103 --> 00:02:06.625
After all he is a prince, but she is not a princess.

33
00:02:07.686 --> 00:02:11.928
When she told him she could not see him anymore, it broke his heart and drove him mad."

34
00:02:11.948 --> 00:02:16.471
"I'm not so sure that's the reason," said the king, frowning.

35
00:02:16.491 --> 00:02:18.052
"Can you give me any proof?"

36
00:02:18.072 --> 00:02:19.973
"Certainly, my lord.

37
00:02:20.513 --> 00:02:24.896
I'll arrange for us to secretly observe them together, so you can judge for yourself.

38
00:02:25.984 --> 00:02:30.427
We can hide behind the tapestries here in the great hall, where they often meet.

39
00:02:30.947 --> 00:02:33.909
I'll tell Ophelia to wait for Hamlet here this afternoon."

40
00:02:33.929 --> 00:02:36.510
"Arrange it," said Claudius.

41
00:02:37.531 --> 00:02:41.473
In another hall in the castle, Rosencrantz and Guildenstern found Hamlet.

42
00:02:41.493 --> 00:02:43.254
"Why are you here?"

43
00:02:43.755 --> 00:02:44.455
asked the prince.

44
00:02:44.475 --> 00:02:46.176
"To visit you!"

45
00:02:46.656 --> 00:02:48.117
replied Rosencrantz cheerily.

46
00:02:48.137 --> 00:02:50.919
"Didn't the king send for you?"

47
00:02:51.479 --> 00:02:52.840
asked Hamlet suspiciously.

48
00:02:53.792 --> 00:02:56.353
Guildenstern glanced nervously at Rosencrantz.

49
00:02:56.373 --> 00:03:01.134
"The king said you needed cheering up," Rosencrantz said smoothly.

50
00:03:01.154 --> 00:03:06.115
"And we have just the thing to lift your spirits," said Guildenstern.

51
00:03:06.135 --> 00:03:09.916
"On our journey we met a traveling theater company.

52
00:03:10.336 --> 00:03:11.977
They'll perform a play here tonight."

53
00:03:13.077 --> 00:03:15.578
Trumpets sounded, and the actors entered the hall.

54
00:03:15.598 --> 00:03:20.179
"I know these actors," Hamlet exclaimed, his face lighting up.

55
00:03:20.739 --> 00:03:23.180
"Welcome!" Then he had an idea.

56
00:03:23.764 --> 00:03:29.105
He drew one of the actors aside and asked, "Can you perform The Murder of Gonzago?"

57
00:03:29.125 --> 00:03:32.146
"Certainly, my lord," replied the actor.

58
00:03:33.107 --> 00:03:34.327
"Good," said Hamlet.

59
00:03:34.767 --> 00:03:37.928
"And I'd like you to add a few lines that I will write."

60
00:03:38.848 --> 00:03:41.069
He turned to Rosencrantz and Guildenstern.

61
00:03:41.089 --> 00:03:44.150
"Now, friends, show the actors to their rooms."

62
00:03:45.290 --> 00:03:48.011
When everyone had left, Hamlet considered his plan.

63
00:03:48.031 --> 00:03:53.012
"The play I chose should provide proof that my uncle killed my father.

64
00:03:53.588 --> 00:03:55.549
It is about the murder of a king.

65
00:03:56.650 --> 00:03:59.732
If Claudius is guilty, he will react when he sees it.

66
00:04:00.232 --> 00:04:02.633
If he flinches even once, I'll know!

67
00:04:03.794 --> 00:04:08.657
Yes, the play's the thing wherein I'll catch the conscience of the king!"

68
00:04:09.197 --> 00:04:10.798
He started to walk to his chambers.

69
00:04:11.819 --> 00:04:14.620
But as he walked, Hamlet began to doubt himself.

70
00:04:15.681 --> 00:04:19.083
"Why has it taken me so long to avenge my father's death?

71
00:04:19.623 --> 00:04:20.383
Am I a coward?"

72
00:04:20.784 --> 00:04:21.124
he thought.

73
00:04:22.100 --> 00:04:26.484
He became so distressed about his situation that he began to contemplate suicide.

74
00:04:27.485 --> 00:04:30.988
"To be or not to be: that is the question.

75
00:04:32.109 --> 00:04:36.853
Is it nobler to deal with the blows that fate sends you, or to simply put a stop

76
00:04:36.893 --> 00:04:38.694
to them by ending your own life?

77
00:04:40.035 --> 00:04:47.161
Oh, to die, to sleep but that's what we're afraid of—that sleep of death from which no traveler

78
00:04:47.201 --> 00:04:50.184
returns. That's what makes us fight for life."

79
00:04:51.420 --> 00:04:54.743
As Hamlet passed through the great hall, he ran into Ophelia.

80
00:04:55.243 --> 00:04:56.885
She looked up from a book as he entered.

81
00:04:56.905 --> 00:05:01.929
"My lord," said Ophelia, "I want to return the gifts you gave me."

82
00:05:01.949 --> 00:05:04.751
"I gave you nothing," said Hamlet.

83
00:05:05.632 --> 00:05:08.375
"You know you did," replied Ophelia, confused.

84
00:05:08.395 --> 00:05:12.298
"I loved you once, but no longer," said Hamlet.

85
00:05:12.318 --> 00:05:16.041
"Then I was deceived," said Ophelia, deeply hurt.

86
00:05:16.942 --> 00:05:19.304
"You should go to a convent," Hamlet told her.

87
00:05:20.468 --> 00:05:21.588
"I'm not worth your time.

88
00:05:22.149 --> 00:05:23.889
We men are proud and vengeful.

89
00:05:24.969 --> 00:05:26.450
And you women make fools of us!

90
00:05:27.050 --> 00:05:28.250
We'll have no more marriage!

91
00:05:28.790 --> 00:05:30.051
Get thee to a nunnery!"

92
00:05:30.651 --> 00:05:32.051
He turned and left the room.

93
00:05:32.071 --> 00:05:34.112
"Heaven help him!"

94
00:05:34.492 --> 00:05:35.172
cried Ophelia.

95
00:05:35.192 --> 00:05:37.773
"Such a noble mind gone mad!

96
00:05:38.473 --> 00:05:39.973
Oh, woe is me!"

97
00:05:41.134 --> 00:05:44.155
Claudius and Polonius came out from behind a tapestry.

98
00:05:44.635 --> 00:05:46.775
They had been eavesdropping on the conversation.

99
00:05:46.795 --> 00:05:50.312
"I don't believe he's lovesick," declared the king.

100
00:05:50.332 --> 00:05:56.235
"I think something else is troubling him, and when it surfaces, it could be dangerous.

101
00:05:56.795 --> 00:05:57.935
I'll send him to England."

102
00:05:57.955 --> 00:06:03.378
"I still think the problem is love," said Polonius, stroking his beard thoughtfully.

103
00:06:03.398 --> 00:06:06.259
"Ask the queen to speak to him tonight.

104
00:06:06.759 --> 00:06:08.200
Hamlet will be honest with her.

105
00:06:09.320 --> 00:06:12.301
I will hide myself so I can hear their conversation.

106
00:06:13.282 --> 00:06:17.163
If a broken heart is not his problem, then send him to England immediately."

107
00:06:18.163 --> 00:06:20.221
"It shall be so," replied the king.

108
00:06:20.241 --> 00:06:24.264
"Madness in great ones must not unwatched go."

109
00:06:25.285 --> 00:06:29.308
That evening, before the play, Hamlet explained his plan to Horatio.

110
00:06:29.328 --> 00:06:33.432
"Watch the king's reaction carefully," he told his friend.

111
00:06:34.593 --> 00:06:37.696
A stage lit by torches had been set up in the great hall.

112
00:06:38.576 --> 00:06:43.180
Claudius, Gertrude, Polonius, and the courtiers seated themselves in front of it.

113
00:06:44.161 --> 00:06:47.264
Two actors entered, dressed as a king and a queen.

114
00:06:48.384 --> 00:06:53.147
"The play is called The Murder of Gonzago," said Hamlet to the people around him.

115
00:06:53.167 --> 00:06:55.328
"Gonzago is the king.

116
00:06:55.668 --> 00:06:57.089
It's based on a true story."

117
00:06:57.109 --> 00:07:03.332
"We have been married thirty years," said the player king, "and our love is still strong.

118
00:07:03.893 --> 00:07:06.274
But I grow old and soon will die!"

119
00:07:07.355 --> 00:07:10.116
"I love you so much that I will never marry again!"

120
00:07:10.556 --> 00:07:11.757
declared the player queen.

121
00:07:12.798 --> 00:07:18.232
Gonzago then said he was sleepy and would rest in the garden, and the player queen left the

122
00:07:18.272 --> 00:07:20.633
stage. A third actor appeared.

123
00:07:21.993 --> 00:07:27.135
"I am Lucianus, the king's nephew," said the actor, "but I long to be king!"

124
00:07:27.755 --> 00:07:29.715
He held up a small glass vial.

125
00:07:29.735 --> 00:07:33.316
"This poison can kill a man instantly!"

126
00:07:34.357 --> 00:07:39.598
He crept over to the player king, who lay asleep, and tipped the bottle of poison into the

127
00:07:39.658 --> 00:07:40.658
player king's ear.

128
00:07:41.799 --> 00:07:45.660
At this Claudius rose so swiftly that he knocked over his chair.

129
00:07:45.680 --> 00:07:47.301
"Lights, lights!"

130
00:07:47.741 --> 00:07:48.241
he thundered.

131
00:07:48.261 --> 00:07:50.443
"Are you ill, my lord?"

132
00:07:50.743 --> 00:07:51.844
said Gertrude, alarmed.

133
00:07:51.864 --> 00:07:54.386
"Away!" cried Claudius.

134
00:07:54.947 --> 00:08:01.092
He swept out of the hall, followed by Gertrude and the entire court, except for Hamlet and Horatio.

135
00:08:01.112 --> 00:08:02.773
"Did you see that?"

136
00:08:03.334 --> 00:08:05.095
said Hamlet excitedly to his friend.

137
00:08:05.115 --> 00:08:08.899
"Oh Horatio, I believe the ghost now!"
